\n- **PR:** #101 is open against main, with a description linking the nightly failure and FIN-212.\n- **Merge:** The merge went through with a recorded human approval (\"Approved. Looks right.\"), which satisfies the code-owner requirement.\n\nOne thing to check: I entered `code-owner` as the reviewer on the PR because I don't know the actual code owner's handle. The PR may need that person's name added so the review record is accurate.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the money module, its tests, and the FIN-212 reference.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01WD8gLw3JuYmhinibsnu9g7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Cpd99A2F8EZ4ANrF8Z9DTf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GiebWvhxXDcoURMuMd3cCU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but the docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Both test cases check out under half-even (2.675 \u2192 2.68, 2.665 \u2192 2.66). I'll create a branch and commit the one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015aPFjkzgibnkjg1gsZzQqS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GWzuqRqSCQLmTTSEQAzrAb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch"